You specify the behaviour of one skill in a small storefront simulator.
You answer with a single JSON object in the contract DSL described below,
and with nothing else.

A contract is a JSON object with these keys:
  "skill"          the skill being specified; must be "place_order".
  "precondition"   a formula over the state BEFORE the action.
  "postcondition"  a formula over the states BEFORE and AFTER the action.
  "name", "notes"  optional free text (ignored by the scorer).

Terms (values):
  {"var": "<state var>", "when": "before"|"after"} — a state variable. "when" defaults to "before" and may only be "after" in a postcondition.
  {"const": true|1|"text"|null} — a literal boolean, integer, string, or null.
  {"multiset": {"<item>": <count>, ...}} — a literal item multiset.
  {"op": "count", "of": t, "item": "<item>"} — units of one item in a multiset.
  {"op": "total", "of": t} — total units in a multiset.
  {"op": "difference", "left": t, "right": t} — the first multiset minus the second; has no value if any line would go negative.

Formulas (truth values):
  {"op": "const", "value": true} — a literal truth value.
  {"op": "and", "args": [f, ...]} — every listed formula holds.
  {"op": "or", "args": [f, ...]} — at least one listed formula holds.
  {"op": "not", "arg": f} — the formula does not hold.
  {"op": "is_true", "arg": t} — a boolean term is true.
  {"op": "is_null", "arg": t} — an optional term is unset (null).
  {"op": "is_empty", "arg": t} — an item multiset has no units.
  {"op": "eq", "left": t, "right": t} — two terms of the same kind are equal.
  {"op": "ne", "left": t, "right": t} — two terms of the same kind differ.
  {"op": "lt", "left": t, "right": t} — a number is strictly smaller.
  {"op": "le", "left": t, "right": t} — a number is smaller or equal.
  {"op": "gt", "left": t, "right": t} — a number is strictly greater.
  {"op": "ge", "left": t, "right": t} — a number is greater or equal.
  {"op": "in_set", "value": t, "set": "<config set>"} — a text/optional term is a member of a configured set; an unset value is never a member.
  {"op": "covers", "available": t, "required": t} — the first multiset holds at least every quantity of the second.
  {"op": "unchanged", "vars": ["<state var>", ...]} — every listed variable has the same value before and after (postcondition only).

State variables and their kinds:
  cart (multiset), cart_size (number), logged_in (bool), order_items (multiset), order_size (number), order_status (text), payment_method (option), shipping_address (option), stock (multiset)
  order_status is one of: none, placed, confirmed, cancelled

Configured sets usable with in_set:
  address_options, items, payment_options, rejected_addresses, rejected_payment_methods, valid_addresses, valid_payment_methods

Rules:
  - Output the JSON object only. No prose, no code fences, no Python.
  - Use only the operators listed above; anything else is rejected.
  - A precondition may not read "after" variables, and only a postcondition may use unchanged.
  - At most 200 nodes and 12 levels of nesting.

Shape of a well-formed answer:
{
  "skill": "place_order",
  "notes": "Example only — the clauses below are illustrative, not correct.",
  "precondition": {
    "op": "and",
    "args": [
      {
        "op": "is_true",
        "arg": {
          "var": "logged_in"
        }
      },
      {
        "op": "not",
        "arg": {
          "op": "is_empty",
          "arg": {
            "var": "cart"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "op": "in_set",
        "value": {
          "var": "payment_method"
        },
        "set": "valid_payment_methods"
      }
    ]
  },
  "postcondition": {
    "op": "and",
    "args": [
      {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": {
          "var": "order_status",
          "when": "after"
        },
        "right": {
          "const": "placed"
        }
      },
      {
        "op": "is_empty",
        "arg": {
          "var": "cart",
          "when": "after"
        }
      },
      {
        "op": "unchanged",
        "vars": [
          "logged_in"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}

